<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n75502" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρχομενός</span></b> , ὁ, also
			ἡ (<i><span class="en">
			Th.
			1.113
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			A.R.
			4.257
		</span></i>), the name of several Greek cities, the most famous of which was
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρχομενὸς Μινύειος</span> in Boeotia,
			<i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.511
		</span></i>, etc.:—Adj.
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρχομένιος</span></b> , <i><span class="en">
			Hp.
			<u>Ulc.</u>
			7
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			9.16
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>SIG</u>
			519.7
		</span></i> (Aegium, <span class="entity">iii B. C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			9.2.40
		</span></i> :—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ὀρχομενίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>side
				with the Orchomenians,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hellanic.
				81
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i> (but perh. not <i><span class="en">
				Hellanic.
			</span></i>).—The old 
				Boeot.
			 form was <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρχ-</span></b> ,
			and this is found in Inscrr. and on coins to the time of Alexander, <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				60
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(v B. C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				7.3166
			</span></i>, al., <i>BMus.Cat.Coins Central Greece</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				p.54
			</span></i>: the Arcadian Orchomenians are similarly 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρχομένιοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					31.12
				</span></i>
			 (Delph., <span class="entity">v B. C.</span>), 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἐρχομίνιοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					5(2).343
				</span></i>
			 (Orchom. <i><span class="en">
				Arc.
			</span></i>, <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>).</div>
